    "problem": "Climate models fail to reproduce the large reduction in ENSO activity during the mid-Holocene suggested by paleoclimate records, as they typically account only for orbital forcing while ignoring crucial changes in Saharan vegetation and dust.",
    "method": "The authors use fully coupled ocean-atmosphere model simulations to demonstrate that accounting for a vegetated and less dusty Sahara during the mid-Holocene reduces El Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation (ENSO) variability by altering the tropical Atlantic mean state, which in turn modifies the Walker circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the impact of a vegetated and less dusty Sahara on El Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation (ENSO) variability during the mid-Holocene using fully coupled ocean-atmosphere model simulations to explain discrepancies between paleoclimate records and previous models.",
